msgid "<span id=\"group-hamiltonian-terms\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Group Hamiltonian terms {#2-group-hamiltonian-terms}"
msgstr "2. I-group ang mga term ng Hamiltonian {#2-group-hamiltonian-terms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the many symmetries that are present in the electronic structure Hamiltonian by grouping related terms that have identical coefficients. This action changes the operator coefficient distribution that the qDRIFT protocol samples from, but it does not affect its convergence guarantees. Crucially, grouping terms that are related by symmetry results in a favorable cancellation of Pauli terms, resulting in an overall shorter circuit depth when time evolving a state under their action.\n"
msgstr "Samantalahin ang maraming symmetry na nasa electronic structure Hamiltonian sa pamamagitan ng pag-group ng magkakaugnay na term na may magkaparehong coefficient. Binabago ng aksyon na ito ang distribusyon ng operator coefficient na sinasample ng qDRIFT protocol, pero hindi nito naaapektuhan ang mga convergence guarantee nito. Mahalaga, ang pag-group ng mga term na magkaugnay sa symmetry ay nagreresulta sa kapaki-pakinabang na pagkansela ng mga Pauli term, kaya mas maikli ang kabuuang circuit depth kapag nag-time evolve ng isang state sa ilalim ng aksyon nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping` module provides convenience functions for grouping an operator’s terms. This is explained in more detail in [this guide](grouping#grouping-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Ang module na `qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping` ay nagbibigay ng mga convenience function para sa pag-group ng mga term ng isang operator. Mas detalyado itong ipinapaliwanag sa [gabay na ito](grouping#grouping-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The implementation of the `group_terms_by_electronic_structure()` assumes the terms of the Hamiltonian to be normal-ordered!\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Pag-iingat\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ipinapalagay ng implementasyon ng `group_terms_by_electronic_structure()` na normal-ordered ang mga term ng Hamiltonian!\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping import group_terms_by_electronic_structure\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.ordering import canonical_order\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> canon = canonical_order(hamil.normal_ordered().simplify(atol=1e-16))\n"
"    >>> exit_code = group_terms_by_electronic_structure(canon, num_modes, two_body_physicist_order=False)\n"
"    >>> assert exit_code is None\n"
"    >>> print(canon.groups)  # the groups attribute now contains some list of group indices\n"
"    [0, ...]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    QfFermionOperator* normal = qf_ferm_op_normal_ordered(hamil, NULL);\n"
"    QfFermionOperator* simplified = qf_ferm_op_simplify(normal, 1e-16);\n"
"    QfFermionOperator* canon = qf_ferm_op_canonical_order(simplified);\n"
"    QfExitCode exit = qf_ferm_op_group_terms_by_electronic_structure(canon, num_modes, false);\n"
"    assert(exit == QfExitCode_Success);\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    qf_ferm_op_free(normal);\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(simplified);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    qf_ferm_op_free(normal);\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(simplified);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Hint\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Pahiwatig\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The full electronic structure Hamiltonian contains certain terms whose inclusion in a time-evolution circuit has no impact on the perceived bitstrings and, thus, only results in an increased sampling overhead. Therefore, it is recommended that such terms be filtered from the Hamiltonian at this point, before constructing the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate in the next step.\n"
msgstr "  Ang buong electronic structure Hamiltonian ay may ilang term na ang pagsama sa isang time-evolution circuit ay walang epekto sa mga bitstring na makikita at, kaya, nagdudulot lang ng dagdag na sampling overhead. Kaya inirerekomendang i-filter ang mga ganoong term mula sa Hamiltonian sa puntong ito, bago buuin ang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate sa susunod na hakbang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The terms that fit this description are those that are diagonal in the occupation-number basis, that is, the products of number operators ($a^\\dagger_i a_i$). This includes the constant energy offset, whose time evolution only introduces a global phase into the circuit, the individual number operators whose time evolution amounts to single-qubit Z rotations, as well as higher-order products such as $n_i n_j$. None of them can change a mode’s occupation, so dropping them costs no excitation content. Unlike the per-draw rejection in step 5, this filtering happens once, on the Hamiltonian itself, so the coefficient distribution the protocol samples from is rebuilt consistently from the filtered operator rather than renormalized mid-draw.\n"
msgstr "  Ang mga term na pasok sa deskripsyong ito ay ang mga diagonal sa occupation-number basis, ibig sabihin, ang mga produkto ng number operator ($a^\\dagger_i a_i$). Kasama rito ang constant energy offset, na ang time evolution ay nagdadala lang ng global phase sa circuit, ang mga indibidwal na number operator na ang time evolution ay katumbas ng single-qubit Z rotation, pati ang mga mas mataas na order na produkto tulad ng $n_i n_j$. Wala sa mga ito ang makapagbabago ng occupation ng isang mode, kaya ang pag-drop sa mga ito ay walang gastos sa excitation content. Hindi tulad ng per-draw rejection sa step 5, nangyayari ang pag-filter na ito nang isang beses, sa mismong Hamiltonian, kaya ang distribusyon ng coefficient na sinasample ng protocol ay muling binubuo nang pare-pareho mula sa na-filter na operator sa halip na i-renormalize sa gitna ng draw.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") function removes such terms from an operator in place:\n"
msgstr "  Ang function na [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") ay nag-aalis ng mga ganoong term mula sa isang operator in place:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  <Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"<TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"
msgstr ""
"  <Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"<TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"
msgstr "<TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"  </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Filtering here, once, is considerably cheaper than filtering repeatedly. [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") runs once per transpiled circuit, so filtering the Hamiltonian initially, rather than on every call, avoids redoing work for every circuit generated from it.\n"
msgstr "  Mas mura nang malaki ang pag-filter dito, nang isang beses lang, kaysa sa paulit-ulit na pag-filter. Tumatakbo nang isang beses ang [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") kada na-transpile na circuit, kaya ang pag-filter sa Hamiltonian sa simula, sa halip na sa bawat tawag, ay iniiwasan ang pag-uulit ng trabaho para sa bawat circuit na nabubuo mula rito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  For the same reason, it pays to order the Hamiltonian’s terms by group index here. Group indices are a per-term tag that says nothing about where those terms sit, so a group’s terms are in general scattered throughout the operator: the grouping applied above assigns indices in order of first encounter, which leaves a group’s second term far from its first.\n"
msgstr "  Dahil sa parehong dahilan, sulit na i-order ang mga term ng Hamiltonian ayon sa group index dito. Ang mga group index ay tag kada term na walang sinasabi kung nasaan ang mga term na iyon, kaya ang mga term ng isang group ay karaniwang nakakalat sa buong operator: ang grouping na inilapat sa itaas ay nagtatalaga ng mga index ayon sa pagkakasunod ng unang pagkakita, kaya malayo ang ikalawang term ng isang group sa una nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") samples whole groups and looks each drawn group up with [`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups\"). Finding a group among scattered terms means scanning all of them, so that lookup costs the same whether one group is drawn or forty. [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_order\") gathers each group into one contiguous run, after which a lookup is a binary search over the group boundaries and costs what the *drawn* groups cost rather than what the *held* terms cost. The lookup itself becomes dramatically cheaper; how much of a given transpilation that saves depends on what else the pipeline does, since mapping and synthesis dominate once the scan is gone:\n"
msgstr "  Sinasample ng [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") ang buong mga group at hinahanap ang bawat nakuhang group gamit ang [`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups\"). Ang paghahanap ng group sa gitna ng nakakalat na mga term ay nangangahulugang pag-scan sa lahat ng mga ito, kaya pareho ang gastos ng paghahanap kahit isa o apatnapung group ang nakuha. Kinokolekta ng [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_order\") ang bawat group sa isang tuloy-tuloy na hanay, kaya pagkatapos nito ang paghahanap ay isang binary search sa mga hangganan ng group at ang gastos ay ayon sa *nakuhang* mga group sa halip na sa *hawak* na mga term. Nagiging napakamura ng mismong paghahanap; kung gaano karami ang natitipid nito sa isang partikular na transpilation ay depende sa iba pang ginagawa ng pipeline, dahil ang mapping at synthesis na ang nangingibabaw kapag wala na ang scan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This reorders the terms without changing the operator’s value, and needs to happen only once no matter how many circuit randomizations are drawn from it.\n"
msgstr "  Inaayos nito ang pagkakasunod ng mga term nang hindi binabago ang halaga ng operator, at kailangan lang itong gawin nang isang beses gaano man karaming circuit randomization ang kukunin mula rito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"prepare-the-time-evolution-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Prepare the time evolution circuit {#3-prepare-the-time-evolution-circuit}"
msgstr "3. Ihanda ang time evolution circuit {#3-prepare-the-time-evolution-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the Hamiltonian’s time evolution circuit and the base circuit from which to draw samples. The [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") contains all the required components to do so, in compliance with Qiskit conventions.\n"
msgstr "Ihanda ang time evolution circuit ng Hamiltonian at ang base circuit na pagkukunan ng mga sample. Ang [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") ay naglalaman ng lahat ng kinakailangang component para rito, alinsunod sa mga convention ng Qiskit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qDRIFT protocol is the synthesis method [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), and the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate carries it as its [`synthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-gate#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate.synthesis \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate.synthesis\"). The method introduces the few parameters you can use to customize the circuits to generate:\n"
msgstr "Ang qDRIFT protocol ang synthesis method na [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), at dala ito ng [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate bilang [`synthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-gate#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate.synthesis \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate.synthesis\") nito. Ipinapakilala ng method ang ilang parameter na magagamit mo para i-customize ang mga circuit na gagawin:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The length of each circuit in terms of excitation groups: `num_groups`\n"
msgstr "Ang haba ng bawat circuit sa mga excitation group: `num_groups`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optionally, a seed for the random number generator: `rng`\n"
msgstr "Opsyonal, isang seed para sa random number generator: `rng`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optionally, precomputed sampling weights, if the transpilation itself becomes a bottleneck: `weights` (see [(Optional) Precompute the sampling weights](#sqdrift-sampling-weights) below)\n"
msgstr "Opsyonal, mga precomputed na sampling weight, kung ang transpilation mismo ang maging bottleneck: `weights` (tingnan ang [(Opsyonal) I-precompute ang mga sampling weight](#sqdrift-sampling-weights) sa ibaba)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the method is held by the gate, whatever describes the gate’s operator, such as those weights, sits right next to that operator.\n"
msgstr "Dahil hawak ng gate ang method, ang anumang naglalarawan sa operator ng gate, tulad ng mga weight na iyon, ay nasa tabi mismo ng operator na iyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit import FermionicCircuit\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit.library import Evolution\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis import FermionicQDrift\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> time = 1.0  # you can choose a desired scaling factor here\n"
"    >>> num_groups = 10\n"
"    >>> qdrift = FermionicQDrift(num_groups, rng=19)\n"
"    >>> evo_gate = Evolution(num_modes, canon, time, synthesis=qdrift)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> circ = FermionicCircuit(num_modes)\n"
"    >>> circ.append(evo_gate, circ.modes)\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // WARNING: Qiskit's C API does not yet allow us to implement circuits\n"
"    // with custom gate definitions.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  This example neither initializes the fermionic modes with particles, nor measures their final state.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Hindi ini-initialize ng halimbawang ito ang mga fermionic mode gamit ang mga particle, at hindi rin nito sinusukat ang huling state nila.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-the-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Transpile the circuit {#4-transpile-the-circuit}"
msgstr "4. I-transpile ang circuit {#4-transpile-the-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_fermions.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler#module-qiskit_fermions.transpiler \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler\") module integrates directly with Qiskit’s transpilation pipeline, allowing the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") constructed above to be directly transpiled to a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"
msgstr "Ang module na [`qiskit_fermions.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler#module-qiskit_fermions.transpiler \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler\") ay direktang isinasama sa transpilation pipeline ng Qiskit, kaya ang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") na binuo sa itaas ay maaaring direktang i-transpile sa isang [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") fermion-to-qubit mapping to convert the Hamiltonian expressed in terms of fermions to be expressed in Pauli strings instead. This can be done directly as part of the transpilation process by using the [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\") transpilation pass. Use [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") to build `FermionicStagedPassManager`, which ensures that the Jordan-Wigner encoding is used consistently for all circuit instructions.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang fermion-to-qubit mapping na [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") para i-convert ang Hamiltonian na nakasaad sa mga fermion para maisaad na lang ito sa mga Pauli string. Magagawa ito nang direkta bilang bahagi ng proseso ng transpilation gamit ang transpilation pass na [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"). Gamitin ang [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") para buuin ang `FermionicStagedPassManager`, na tinitiyak na pare-pareho ang paggamit ng Jordan-Wigner encoding sa lahat ng circuit instruction.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Crucially, add Qiskit’s [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) pass to the `optimization` stage of the transpilation pipeline. It breaks the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate down with the synthesis method the gate carries, which is the qDRIFT method prepared above. This ensures that the circuit does not use the time evolution of the entire Hamiltonian, whose depth would exceed the capabilities of currently available quantum computing hardware.\n"
msgstr "Mahalaga, idagdag ang [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) pass ng Qiskit sa `optimization` stage ng transpilation pipeline. Binabaklas nito ang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate gamit ang synthesis method na dala ng gate, na siyang qDRIFT method na inihanda sa itaas. Tinitiyak nito na hindi gagamitin ng circuit ang time evolution ng buong Hamiltonian, na ang depth ay lalampas sa kakayahan ng kasalukuyang magagamit na quantum computing hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead, it subsamples a fixed number of `groups` of Hamiltonian terms for each circuit, every time the circuit is transpiled. Through this, you can generate multiple circuit randomizations as required by the [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) algorithm by repeatedly running the transpilation pipeline. The number of circuits to generate is `num_sqdrift_randomizations`.\n"
msgstr "Sa halip, nagsa-subsample ito ng takdang bilang ng `groups` ng mga term ng Hamiltonian para sa bawat circuit, tuwing ita-transpile ang circuit. Dahil dito, makakagawa ka ng maraming circuit randomization ayon sa kinakailangan ng algorithm na [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) sa pamamagitan ng paulit-ulit na pagpapatakbo ng transpilation pipeline. Ang bilang ng mga circuit na gagawin ay `num_sqdrift_randomizations`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit.transpiler.passes import Decompose\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler import FermionicPassManager\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets import generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> pm = generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()\n"
"    >>> pm.optimization = FermionicPassManager([Decompose([\"Evolution\"])])\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> num_sqdrift_randomizations = 10\n"
"    >>> sqdrift_circuits = [\n"
"    ...     pm.run(circ) for _ in range(num_sqdrift_randomizations)\n"
"    ... ]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // WARNING: Qiskit's C API does not yet allow us to implement circuits\n"
"    // with custom gate definitions, which we therefore also cannot transpile\n"
"    // via this API.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The preceding examples fix the `rng` seed of the [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") synthesis method, so that the sequence of randomizations can be reproduced.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Itinatakda ng mga naunang halimbawa ang `rng` seed ng synthesis method na [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), para maulit ang pagkakasunod ng mga randomization.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The same pipeline accepts the qDRIFT method in two other places. The [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass takes one method for *every* [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate by name, `F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": FermionicQDrift(num_groups)})`, which is all that is needed when no gate holds anything specific to its operator. The next step uses the third one, the [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") pass.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Pahiwatig\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Tumatanggap ang parehong pipeline ng qDRIFT method sa dalawa pang lugar. Ang pass na [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") ay kumukuha ng isang method para sa *bawat* [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate ayon sa pangalan, `F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": FermionicQDrift(num_groups)})`, na siyang sapat kapag walang gate na may hawak na partikular sa operator nito. Ang ikatlo ay gagamitin sa susunod na hakbang, ang pass na [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"filter-drawn-excitations-by-occupation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Filter drawn excitations by occupation {#5-filter-drawn-excitations-by-occupation}"
msgstr "5. I-filter ang mga nakuhang excitation ayon sa occupation {#5-filter-drawn-excitations-by-occupation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beyond the diagonal terms filtered out in the previous step, a drawn excitation can act entirely within a set of modes whose occupation is already fixed (all occupied or all unoccupied), where it cannot move a particle from one side to the other. Such an excitation tells you nothing about the sampled bitstrings, so a slot spent on it is a slot wasted. The [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") pass, which wraps the same [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") method, rejects such excitations as they are drawn and draws a replacement, so that each of the `num_groups` slots of the resulting circuit carries an excitation that couples the two sides.\n"
msgstr "Bukod sa mga diagonal term na na-filter sa nakaraang hakbang, ang isang nakuhang excitation ay maaaring kumilos nang buo sa loob ng isang set ng mga mode na ayos na ang occupation (lahat occupied o lahat unoccupied), kung saan hindi ito makapaglilipat ng particle mula sa isang panig patungo sa kabila. Walang sinasabi sa iyo ang ganoong excitation tungkol sa mga na-sample na bitstring, kaya sayang ang slot na ginugol dito. Ang pass na [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\"), na bumabalot sa parehong method na [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), ay tumatanggi sa mga ganoong excitation habang kinukuha ang mga ito at kumukuha ng kapalit, kaya ang bawat isa sa `num_groups` slot ng resultang circuit ay may excitation na nag-uugnay sa dalawang panig.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  This filtering is not free, and it is a separate pass for that reason. What it conserves is the budget of `num_groups` sampled slots, not the circuit depth: since that budget is fixed, a rejected excitation is replaced rather than dropped, and a cheap one gives way to a coupling excitation that costs more to synthesize. Expect a filtered circuit to be deeper than an unfiltered one drawn from the same seed.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Babala\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Hindi libre ang pag-filter na ito, at hiwalay itong pass dahil dito. Ang pinapanatili nito ay ang badyet ng `num_groups` na sampled slot, hindi ang circuit depth: dahil nakapirmi ang badyet na iyon, pinapalitan ang tinanggihang excitation sa halip na tanggalin, at ang mura ay napapalitan ng coupling excitation na mas magastos i-synthesize. Asahan na mas malalim ang na-filter na circuit kaysa sa hindi na-filter na kinuha mula sa parehong seed.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Renormalizing the draw over the accepted excitations changes the distribution the qDRIFT protocol samples from, and unlike the grouping in step 2 it also breaks the protocol’s convergence guarantee: the sampled product no longer averages to the evolution under the Hamiltonian you passed in. Every retained excitation ends up weighted by the reciprocal of the acceptance probability, the rejected ones contribute nothing, and neither the total coefficient magnitude nor the per-gate evolution time is adjusted to compensate.\n"
msgstr "  Ang pag-renormalize ng draw sa mga tinanggap na excitation ay nagbabago sa distribusyon na sinasample ng qDRIFT protocol, at hindi tulad ng grouping sa step 2, sinisira rin nito ang convergence guarantee ng protocol: ang na-sample na produkto ay hindi na nag-a-average sa evolution sa ilalim ng Hamiltonian na ipinasa mo. Ang bawat natirang excitation ay nabibigyan ng bigat na katumbas ng reciprocal ng acceptance probability, ang mga tinanggihan ay walang naiaambag, at hindi inaayos ang kabuuang laki ng coefficient o ang evolution time kada gate para bumawi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The acceptance rule is also an over-approximation. It compares mode supports only, so it carries no amplitude information, and the tracked sets only ever grow: an excitation confined to the occupied set is genuinely inert on a product state, but the same reasoning gets weaker for later draws, once earlier accepted excitations have left the state entangled and marked most modes “uncertain”.\n"
msgstr "  Isang over-approximation din ang acceptance rule. Mode supports lang ang kinukumpara nito, kaya wala itong dalang amplitude information, at lumalaki lang ang mga tracked set: ang excitation na nakakulong sa occupied set ay talagang inert sa isang product state, pero humihina ang parehong katwiran para sa mga susunod na draw, kapag ang mga naunang tinanggap na excitation ay nag-iwan sa state na entangled at minarkahan ang karamihan ng mga mode bilang “uncertain”.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use the filtering for the bitstring-sampling workflow this guide describes, where the circuits feed SQD post-processing and only the sampled bitstrings matter. Do not use it if you intend to estimate an expectation value from these circuits, or to rely on the qDRIFT error bound in any other way: those results carry a bias that the pass does not correct for.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Gamitin ang pag-filter para sa bitstring-sampling workflow na inilalarawan ng gabay na ito, kung saan ang mga circuit ay pinapasok sa SQD post-processing at ang mga na-sample na bitstring lang ang mahalaga. Huwag itong gamitin kung balak mong tantiyahin ang isang expectation value mula sa mga circuit na ito, o umasa sa qDRIFT error bound sa anumang ibang paraan: ang mga resultang iyon ay may bias na hindi itinatama ng pass.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This filtering needs to know which modes start out occupied. It therefore requires an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate preceding the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates in the circuit; [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") is a convenient way to construct one. Add one here for the N2 Hartree-Fock reference (seven alpha and seven beta electrons in 14 spatial orbitals) and compare the sampled excitations with and without the filtering:\n"
msgstr "Kailangang malaman ng pag-filter na ito kung aling mga mode ang occupied sa simula. Kaya nangangailangan ito ng [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate bago ang mga [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate sa circuit; ang [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") ay madaling paraan para bumuo nito. Magdagdag ng isa rito para sa N2 Hartree-Fock reference (pitong alpha at pitong beta na electron sa 14 na spatial orbital) at ihambing ang mga na-sample na excitation na may at walang pag-filter:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit.library import InitializeModes\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes import F2FSynthesis, QDriftTrotterization\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> init = InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock(fcidump.norb, (7, 7))\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> hf_circ = FermionicCircuit(num_modes)\n"
"    >>> hf_circ.append(init, hf_circ.modes)\n"
"    >>> hf_circ.append(Evolution(num_modes, canon, time), hf_circ.modes)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> num_groups = 5\n"
"    >>> qdrift_unfiltered = F2FSynthesis(\n"
"    ...     {\"Evolution\": FermionicQDrift(num_groups, rng=3480)}\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>> qdrift_trivial = QDriftTrotterization(\n"
"    ...     FermionicQDrift(num_groups, rng=3480)\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> for instruction in FermionicPassManager(qdrift_unfiltered).run(hf_circ)._inner.data:\n"
"    ...     if instruction.operation.name == \"Evolution\":\n"
"    ...         print(sorted(instruction.operation.operator.get_support()))\n"
"    [2, 4]\n"
"    [41, 45, 52]\n"
"    [15, 45, 55]\n"
"    [41, 52, 53]\n"
"    [10, 16, 37, 38]\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> for instruction in FermionicPassManager(qdrift_trivial).run(hf_circ)._inner.data:\n"
"    ...     if instruction.operation.name == \"Evolution\":\n"
"    ...         print(sorted(instruction.operation.operator.get_support()))\n"
"    [0, 1, 6, 7]\n"
"    [0, 1, 28, 29]\n"
"    [4, 13, 55]\n"
"    [13, 20, 40, 41]\n"
"    [0, 1, 28, 29]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "None of the excitations drawn without filtering touch the occupied set (`0-6` and `28-34`) at all, so none of them can move a particle between an occupied and an unoccupied mode. With the filtering, all five are rejected and replaced by excitations that do couple an occupied mode with an unoccupied one. For example, the first accepted excitation `[0, 1, 6, 7]` moves a particle between occupied modes `0`, `1`, and `6` and unoccupied mode `7`.\n"
msgstr "Wala sa mga excitation na nakuha nang walang pag-filter ang humahawak sa occupied set (`0-6` at `28-34`), kaya wala sa mga ito ang makapaglilipat ng particle sa pagitan ng occupied at unoccupied na mode. Sa pag-filter, lahat ng lima ay tinanggihan at pinalitan ng mga excitation na nag-uugnay nga ng occupied na mode sa unoccupied na mode. Halimbawa, ang unang tinanggap na excitation na `[0, 1, 6, 7]` ay naglilipat ng particle sa pagitan ng mga occupied na mode na `0`, `1`, at `6` at ng unoccupied na mode na `7`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once an excitation is accepted, every mode in its support becomes “uncertain” and, thus, eligible to play either role for later samples, so the occupied and unoccupied mode sets keep growing as more excitations get accepted. This is what makes the second excitation, `[0, 1, 28, 29]`, acceptable. All four of its modes are among the *originally* occupied ones, so it does not couple to any originally unoccupied mode. It is only accepted because modes `0` and `1` became uncertain (and thus eligible as the “unoccupied” side of the coupling) once the first excitation touched them.\n"
msgstr "Kapag natanggap ang isang excitation, ang bawat mode sa support nito ay nagiging “uncertain” at, kaya, puwedeng gumanap ng alinmang papel para sa mga susunod na sample, kaya patuloy na lumalaki ang mga set ng occupied at unoccupied na mode habang mas maraming excitation ang natatanggap. Ito ang dahilan kung bakit katanggap-tanggap ang ikalawang excitation, `[0, 1, 28, 29]`. Ang lahat ng apat nitong mode ay kabilang sa mga *orihinal* na occupied, kaya hindi ito nag-uugnay sa anumang orihinal na unoccupied na mode. Tinanggap lang ito dahil naging uncertain ang mga mode na `0` at `1` (kaya puwede nang maging “unoccupied” na panig ng coupling) nang mahawakan sila ng unang excitation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This growth is what makes the rule an over-approximation rather than a test: as more modes turn uncertain, fewer draws are rejected, and the filtering does the most to the sampling distribution on the earliest draws.\n"
msgstr "Ang paglaking ito ang dahilan kung bakit over-approximation ang rule at hindi isang test: habang mas maraming mode ang nagiging uncertain, mas kaunting draw ang tinatanggihan, at ang pag-filter ang may pinakamalaking epekto sa sampling distribution sa mga pinakaunang draw.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To judge how far the filtering moved the distribution, read the rejection counts the pass records in the circuit metadata. One entry is stored per filtered [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, and the accepted-to-total ratio estimates the acceptance probability, which is the factor by which the retained excitations were over-weighted:\n"
msgstr "Para masukat kung gaano kalayo ang nailipat ng pag-filter sa distribusyon, basahin ang mga rejection count na itinatala ng pass sa circuit metadata. Isang entry ang iniimbak kada na-filter na [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, at ang ratio ng tinanggap sa kabuuan ay tumatantiya sa acceptance probability, na siyang salik kung saan na-over-weight ang mga natirang excitation:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> # a freshly seeded pass, so the counts do not depend on earlier draws\n"
"    >>> qdrift_counted = QDriftTrotterization(\n"
"    ...     FermionicQDrift(num_groups, rng=3480)\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>> filtered = FermionicPassManager(qdrift_counted).run(hf_circ)\n"
"    >>> discarded = filtered.metadata.get(\"filter_trivial.discarded\")\n"
"    >>> emitted = filtered.metadata.get(\"filter_trivial.emitted\")\n"
"    >>> print(f\"{emitted[0]} kept, {discarded[0]} discarded\")\n"
"    5 kept, 7 discarded\n"
"    >>> print(f\"acceptance probability: {emitted[0] / (emitted[0] + discarded[0]):.2f}\")\n"
"    acceptance probability: 0.42\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Filtering needs occupation information to filter against. A [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate seeds it just as [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") does, and any [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") marks every mode it acts on as “uncertain”. Without any of them, or when the seeded modes all land on one side (every mode occupied, or every mode unoccupied), the pass emits a [`UserWarning`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#UserWarning) and leaves the sampling unfiltered for that [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate. On a Hamiltonian whose remaining terms can no longer couple the two tracked sets, the pass instead raises [`RuntimeError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#RuntimeError) after [`QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES\") consecutive rejections.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kailangan ng pag-filter ng occupation information na pagbabatayan. Ang [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate ay nagbibigay nito gaya ng [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), at minamarkahan ng anumang [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") ang bawat mode na kinikilos nito bilang “uncertain”. Kung wala ni isa sa mga ito, o kapag ang lahat ng seeded na mode ay napunta sa isang panig (lahat occupied, o lahat unoccupied), maglalabas ang pass ng [`UserWarning`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#UserWarning) at iiwang hindi na-filter ang sampling para sa [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate na iyon. Sa Hamiltonian na ang natitirang mga term ay hindi na makapag-uugnay sa dalawang tracked set, ang pass ay magtataas na lang ng [`RuntimeError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#RuntimeError) pagkatapos ng magkakasunod na pagtanggi na umabot sa [`QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sqdrift-sampling-weights\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) Precompute the sampling weights {#optional-precompute-the-sampling-weights}"
msgstr "(Opsyonal) I-precompute ang mga sampling weight {#optional-precompute-the-sampling-weights}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reach for this only if the transpilation itself is a bottleneck. It changes nothing about the circuits you get.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin lang ito kung ang transpilation mismo ang bottleneck. Wala itong binabago sa mga circuit na makukuha mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") draws each group with a probability proportional to the magnitude of its coefficient, and derives those magnitudes from the Hamiltonian on every call: one value per Hamiltonian *term*, reduced down to one per group. Because the method is stateless it repeats that reduction for every randomization, even though the result is identical every time. The `weights` argument lets you compute it once with [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") and hand the result over, moving the cost out of the loop while leaving the method free of any cached, Hamiltonian-dependent state.\n"
msgstr "Kinukuha ng [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") ang bawat group na may probabilidad na proporsyonal sa laki ng coefficient nito, at kinukuha ang mga laki na iyon mula sa Hamiltonian sa bawat tawag: isang halaga kada *term* ng Hamiltonian, na binabawasan hanggang isa kada group. Dahil stateless ang method, inuulit nito ang reduction na iyon sa bawat randomization, kahit pareho ang resulta tuwing gagawin. Hinahayaan ka ng argumentong `weights` na i-compute ito nang isang beses gamit ang [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") at ipasa ang resulta, na inilalabas ang gastos sa loop habang walang naka-cache na state na nakadepende sa Hamiltonian ang method.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the counterpart of the term ordering in step 2. That one hoists the group *lookup* out of the loop, this one the weight *reduction*, and each is only as noticeable as the other is absent, so it is worth applying both together. Since `canon` was already reordered above, the two compose directly.\n"
msgstr "Ito ang katapat ng term ordering sa step 2. Inilalabas niyon ang group *lookup* sa loop, ito naman ang weight *reduction*, at kapansin-pansin ang bawat isa ayon lang sa kawalan ng isa pa, kaya sulit na ilapat ang dalawa nang magkasama. Dahil ang `canon` ay na-reorder na sa itaas, direkta silang nagkakasundo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The weights describe the groups of one particular operator, so they belong with the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate of that operator: build the method for that gate and hand it over as the gate’s `synthesis`, exactly as in step 3.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga weight ay naglalarawan sa mga group ng isang partikular na operator, kaya kabilang sila sa [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate ng operator na iyon: buuin ang method para sa gate na iyon at ipasa ito bilang `synthesis` ng gate, gaya mismo sa step 3.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping import group_coeff_means\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> weights = group_coeff_means(canon)  # `canon` is group-ordered, from step 2\n"
"    >>> qdrift_weighted = FermionicQDrift(10, rng=19, weights=weights)\n"
"    >>> weighted_gate = Evolution(num_modes, canon, time, synthesis=qdrift_weighted)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> weighted_circ = FermionicCircuit(num_modes)\n"
"    >>> weighted_circ.append(weighted_gate, weighted_circ.modes)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> weighted_circuits = [\n"
"    ...     pm.run(weighted_circ) for _ in range(num_sqdrift_randomizations)\n"
"    ... ]\n"
"    >>> len(weighted_circuits)\n"
"    10\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since those are exactly the weights the pass would have computed, the circuits are the same as before; only the repeated reduction is gone.\n"
msgstr "Dahil ito mismo ang mga weight na ico-compute ng pass, pareho ang mga circuit sa dati; ang paulit-ulit na reduction lang ang nawala.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One entry is expected per *group*, not per term, whenever the operator carries groups, since a grouped operator is sampled group-wise. Entries must be non-negative: a weight is a *magnitude*, because the qDRIFT protocol decomposes $H = \\sum_j h_j H_j$ with positive $h_j$, and a coefficient’s sign belongs to $H_j$, where the pass reads it off the operator directly.\n"
msgstr "Isang entry ang inaasahan kada *group*, hindi kada term, tuwing may mga group ang operator, dahil ang grouped na operator ay sinasample kada group. Dapat hindi negatibo ang mga entry: ang weight ay isang *magnitude*, dahil dinedecompose ng qDRIFT protocol ang $H = \\sum_j h_j H_j$ na may positibong $h_j$, at ang sign ng coefficient ay kabilang sa $H_j$, kung saan direktang binabasa ito ng pass mula sa operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The weights are absolute magnitudes, not relative preferences. Their sum also fixes the evolution time, so multiplying every entry by $\\gamma$ samples identically but evolves for $\\gamma t$ instead of $t$. Passing anything other than the Hamiltonian’s own coefficient magnitudes therefore changes which evolution the ensemble approximates, which is why this is a performance tool rather than a way to tune the sampling.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Pag-iingat\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang mga weight ay absolute magnitude, hindi relatibong kagustuhan. Ang kabuuan nila ang nagtatakda rin ng evolution time, kaya ang pagpaparami ng bawat entry sa $\\gamma$ ay pareho ang sampling pero nag-e-evolve ng $\\gamma t$ sa halip na $t$. Kaya ang pagpasa ng anumang bukod sa sariling coefficient magnitude ng Hamiltonian ay nagbabago kung aling evolution ang tinatantiya ng ensemble, kaya isa itong performance tool at hindi paraan para i-tune ang sampling.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the weights belong to the gate whose operator they describe, a circuit may hold several [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates, each with the weights of its own operator. The [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") pass of step 5 honors them in the same way: it draws a gate with the [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") that the gate carries, and falls back to the one it was constructed with for the gates that carry none. Another kind of synthesis method on a gate is not a statement about qDRIFT, so the pass ignores it. Giving the method to a pass by gate name instead, as in `F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": ...})`, applies one method to every [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, so weights passed there are only meaningful for a circuit with a single one. The length of the weights is checked against each gate they are applied to.\n"
msgstr "Dahil ang mga weight ay kabilang sa gate na ang operator ay inilalarawan nila, ang isang circuit ay maaaring may ilang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, bawat isa ay may mga weight ng sarili nitong operator. Ang pass na [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") ng step 5 ay sumusunod din dito sa parehong paraan: kumukuha ito ng gate gamit ang [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") na dala ng gate, at bumabalik sa ginamit sa pagkakabuo nito para sa mga gate na walang dala. Ang ibang uri ng synthesis method sa isang gate ay hindi pahayag tungkol sa qDRIFT, kaya hindi ito pinapansin ng pass. Ang pagbibigay ng method sa pass ayon sa pangalan ng gate, tulad ng sa `F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": ...})`, ay nagpapatupad ng isang method sa bawat [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, kaya ang mga weight na ipinasa roon ay makabuluhan lang para sa circuit na may iisa lang. Sinusuri ang haba ng mga weight laban sa bawat gate na pinaglalapatan nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) Optimize the fermionic mode indexing {#optional-optimize-the-fermionic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr "(Opsyonal) I-optimize ang fermionic mode indexing {#optional-optimize-the-fermionic-mode-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can add an additional optimization step to the transpilation pipeline that minimizes the distance of the fermionic excitation spans by relabeling the fermionic mode indices. This optimization was introduced in the [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) paper and is implemented by [`build_excitation_span_minimization_model()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-optimization-build-excitation-span-minimization-model#qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model\"). It can be easily inserted into the transpiler pipeline by using the [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") pass:\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang magdagdag ng karagdagang optimization step sa transpilation pipeline na nagpapaliit sa distansya ng mga fermionic excitation span sa pamamagitan ng pag-relabel ng mga fermionic mode index. Ipinakilala ang optimization na ito sa paper na [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) at ipinapatupad ng [`build_excitation_span_minimization_model()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-optimization-build-excitation-span-minimization-model#qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model\"). Madali itong maisingit sa transpiler pipeline gamit ang pass na [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\"):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from pyomo.environ import SolverFactory\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes import RelabelModes\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> solver = SolverFactory(\"appsi_highs\")\n"
"    >>> solver.options[\"time_limit\"] = 10\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> qdrift = F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": FermionicQDrift(5, rng=19)})\n"
"    >>> relabel = RelabelModes(solver=solver)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> pm.optimization = FermionicPassManager([qdrift, relabel])\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> relabeled_circ = pm.run(circ)\n"
"    >>> # if the automatic mode relabeling was successful, the circuit's\n"
"    >>> # metadata will contain the mode `permutation` information\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // WARNING: This feature is not available via the C API.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Using the automatic optimization inside [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (which leverages [`build_excitation_span_minimization_model()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-optimization-build-excitation-span-minimization-model#qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model\")) requires the optional dependency managed by [`HAS_PYOMO`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_PYOMO \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_PYOMO\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang paggamit ng awtomatikong optimization sa loob ng [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (na gumagamit ng [`build_excitation_span_minimization_model()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-optimization-build-excitation-span-minimization-model#qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model\")) ay nangangailangan ng opsyonal na dependency na pinamamahalaan ng [`HAS_PYOMO`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_PYOMO \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_PYOMO\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The relabeling changes which mode a given qubit carries, so the subspace diagonalization only gets the right bitstrings if that is accounted for. Where the accounting happens depends on where you measure.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Mahalaga\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Binabago ng relabeling kung aling mode ang dala ng isang qubit, kaya makukuha lang ng subspace diagonalization ang tamang mga bitstring kung isasaalang-alang ito. Nakadepende kung saan ito isinasaalang-alang sa kung saan ka sumusukat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Add the measurements to the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") with [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") before transpiling, and there is nothing to do: each measurement names the mode it reads, so the relabeling carries it along and the sampled bitstrings are indexed by the original mode.\n"
msgstr "  Idagdag ang mga measurement sa [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") gamit ang [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") bago mag-transpile, at wala nang ibang gagawin: pinangalanan ng bawat measurement ang mode na binabasa nito, kaya dala ito ng relabeling at ang mga na-sample na bitstring ay naka-index ayon sa orihinal na mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Measure the transpiled [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) instead, and the bitstrings must be post-processed using the `permutation` recorded in the circuit’s metadata. See the [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") documentation for the recipe.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kung ang na-transpile na [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) ang susukatin mo, kailangang i-post-process ang mga bitstring gamit ang `permutation` na naitala sa metadata ng circuit. Tingnan ang dokumentasyon ng [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") para sa recipe.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

